  "starterCode": "import torch\n\ndef dl_unet(encoder_feat: list, decoder_feat: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **U-Net Skip Connection** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport torch\n\ndef dl_unet(encoder_feat: list, decoder_feat: list) -> list:\n    enc = torch.tensor(encoder_feat, dtype=torch.float32)\n    dec = torch.tensor(decoder_feat, dtype=torch.float32)\n    dh = (enc.shape[2] - dec.shape[2]) // 2\n    dw = (enc.shape[3] - dec.shape[3]) // 2\n    enc_cropped = enc[:, :, dh:dh+dec.shape[2], dw:dw+dec.shape[3]]\n    return torch.cat([enc_cropped, dec], dim=1).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
